NO. †*227 \n \n TO BE ANSWERED ON THE 01ST AUGUST, 2017 / SHRAVANA 10, 1939 (SAKA) \n \n  VACANT POSTS OF IPS OFFICERS \n \n  †*227.  SHRI KIRTI AZAD: \n \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state:    \n \n(a) the number of sanctioned posts of  the Indian Police Service (IPS) officers in  \nthe country; \n \n(b) the basis of fixing the number of sanctioned posts of IPS; \n \n(c) the number of posts of IPS office rs filled up along with the number of  \nvacancies at present; \n \n(d) the number of sanctioned posts of  IPS officers and the number of such posts  \nlying vacant in Bihar at present; and \n \n(e) the steps taken by the Government  to fill up all the vacant posts of IPS  \nofficers in the country including Bihar? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n(SHRI KIREN RIJIJU) \n \n(a) to (e):   A statement is laid on the table of the House. \n \n \n \n \n\n \n--2-- \nStatement as referred to in reply to parts (a) to (e) of the Lok Sabha Starred \nQuestion No. *227 for answer on 01.08.2017 regarding  “ Vacant Posts of IPS \nOfficers”. \n \n(a) As on 01/01/2017, the authorised strength of IPS officers in the country is \n4843. \n(b) Fixing the number of sanctioned posts of IPS depends upon functional \nrequirement of a particular cadre.  As per rule 4 (2) of IPS Cadre Rules, 1954, the \nCentral Government, ordinarily at the interval of every five years, reviews the \nstrength and compositi on of each such cadre in consultation with the State \nGovernment(s) concerned and revises the authorised strength of the IPS for \neach Cadre.  \n(c) As on 01.01.2017, 3905 IPS are in position against authorized strength of \n4843 IPS officers. There are 938 vaca ncies in the Indian Police Service as on \n01.01.2017. \n(d) As on 01.01.2017, 189 IPS officers are in position against authorised \nstrength of 231 officers in IPS Cadre of Bihar. As such, there are 42 vacancies. \n(e) To fill up the vacancies of IPS officers, the batch-size