K  SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.214 FOR 31.7.2017 \n \n \n(a) There are 3686 monuments/sites including temples which have been \ndeclared as protected monuments/sites in the country with 285 \nmonuments/sites in Maharashtra.  \n \n(b) The revenue earned from sale of entry t ickets at the centrally protected \nticketed monuments under Archaeological Survey of India during the year \n2016-17 is Rs.221.30 crores.  \n \n(c) The Ministry of Culture has recommended prohibition on use of polythene. \nASI has declared all ASI protected Monume nts and Archaeological Sites as \n‘Polythene Free Zone’.   \n \n(d) No such proposal is under consideration. \n \n \n \n \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|12|UNSTARRED |215", "t": "Promotion of FDI", "head": "(c)  \n \nThe Science Cities Scheme provides for setting up of Science Cities \nand Science Centres in all the states of the country, subject to \navailability of funds for this purpose. Stat\nes willing to avail of this \nScheme have to provide land and share the cost of setting up of \nfacility and corpus for upkeep and maintenance.  \n \n \nThe Science Centres set up in the states of Bihar, Jharkhand, \nRajasthan and Gujarat are:\n \n��\n��\n��\n��\nSri Krishna Science Cen\ntre,Patna, \n����������\n��\n2\n.\n \nRegional Science Centre, Ranchi, \n������������������\n \n3\n.\n \nRegional Science Centre, Jaipur, \n������������������\n \n4\n.\n \nSub\n-\nRegional Science Centre, Jodhpur, \n������������������\n \n5\n.\n \nDistrict Science Centre, Dharampur\n��������������������\n \n \nThe proposals to set up Sub Regional Science Centre, Udaipu\nr in \nRajasth\nan, Sub Regional Science Centre\n,\n \nGaya and  Dr. A. P. J. \nAbdul  Kalam Science City, Patna in Bihar have been approved by \nMinistry of Culture. \n \n \nThere is no specific time frame in the Scheme in which Science \nCities/Science Centres are to be set u\np in each State/UT, since setting \nup of a Science City/Science Centre depends on the receipt of a \nproposal from S