 AAY stands at 2.50 crore \nfamilies. \n \n Under NFSA, AAY families are entitled to receive 35 Kg of \nfoodgrains per family per month at a highly subsidized rate of Rs.3/2/1- per \nkg for rice, wheat and coarse grains respectively. The identification of \nAAY families, against the State/UT -wise allocated number of households, \nis the responsibility of the concerned State/UT, as per the \ncriteria/guidelines issued by the Central Government. The criteria for \nidentification of AAY families inter -alia, include, households headed by \nwidows, terminally ill persons, disabled persons, primitive tribal \nhouseholds, eligible BPL families of HIV positive persons, marginal \nfarmers etc. States/UTs wise details of total number of families covered \nunder AAY are at Annexure-I.  \n \n The States/UTs-wise and year wise details of  allocation and offtake \nof foodgrains for the last three years and current year is at Annexure-II. \n***  \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nANNEXURE -I \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (d) OF THE STARRED QUESTION NO. 313 DUE FOR ANSWER ON 08.08.2017 IN THE  LOK SABHA \n \nStates/UTs wise and year-wise list of details of identified families under Antyodaya Anna Yojana  (AAY) since 2001-02 to 2017-18 \n                   \n                            \n \n  \n(fig. In lakh) \nS.No. States/UTs 2001-02 2002-03 2003-04 2004-05 2005-06 2006-07 2007-08 2008-09 2009-10 2010-11 2011-12 2012-13 2013-14 2014-15 2015-16 2016-17 \n2017-18 as on \n24.07.2017 \n1 Andhra Pd* 6.228 6.228 9.345 12.336 15.578 15.578 15.578 15.578 15.578 15.578 15.578 15.578 15.578 15.578 9.080 9.080 9.08 \n2 Arunachal Pd 0.151 0.151 0.151 0.301 0.380 0.38 0.38 0.38 0.38 0.38 0.38 0.38 0.38 0.38 0.370 0.370 0.37 \n3 Assam 2.815 2.815 2.815 2.815 5.575 7.005 7.04 7.04 7.04 7.04 7.04 7.04 7.04 7.04 7.000 7.002 7.00 \n4 Bihar 10.000 10.000 10 10 15.003 24.134 24.285 24.285 24.285 25.010 25.010 25.010 25.01 25.01 25.010 25.010 25.01 \n5 Chattisgarh 2.874 