conut farmers of the \nKonaseema\n \nregion including the farmers of East and West Godavari districts due to rapid \ndecline in the prices of tender coconut; \n \n \n(b) \n \nif so, the details thereof; and \n \n \n(c)\n \n \nthe steps taken by the Government to provide relief to the farmers of the region?\n \n \n \nANSWER\n \nMINISTER OF AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n  \n½ãâ¨ããè\n \n \n \n \n  \n(SHRI RADHA MOHAN SINGH\n)\n \n \n \n(a) to (\nc\n):\n \nA statement is laid on the Table of the House.\n \n \n \n \n \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (\nc\n) OF L\nOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.\n  \n314  \nDUE FOR REPLY ON\n  \n8\nTH\n  \nAUGUST, 2017\n.\n \n(a) & (b):\n \nThe price of tender coconut in West Godavari region during July 2017 was \nranging between Rs.7/\n-\n \nto Rs.8/\n-\n \nper nut which is slightly higher than the price of tender \ncoconut which ranged between Rs.6/\n-\n \nt\no Rs.7/\n-\n \nper nut during July 2016. \n \n(c): \n \n   \nMinistry of Agriculture and Farmers’ Welfare through \nCoconut Development \nBoard (CDB) is implementing various schemes in Andhra Pradesh with a view to \nencourage value addition and byproduct utilization through Fa\nrmer Producer \nOrganizations (FPOs). CDB is facilitating the formation of FPOs in coconut sector for \nthe benefit of coconut farmers.  \n \n \n \nIn order to help the coconut farmers in getting remunerative prices for their \nproduce, the Central Government has been i\nmplementing \nPrice Support Scheme (PSS) \nfor procurement of oil seeds, pulses and cotton through Central nodal agencies.\n \nThis \nscheme is implemented at the request of the concerned State Government which \nagrees to exempt the procured commodities from levy of \nmandi tax and assist central \nnodal agencies in logistic arrangements, including gunny bags, working capital for state \nagencies, creation of revolving fund for PSS operations, etc. as required under the \nscheme guidelines. The procurement of oilseeds, pulses\n \n& cotton are undertaken by \ncentral agencies at Minimum Support Price (MSP) announced by the Government as \nand when prices fall below the MSP.\n \nIn addition to above Price Support Scheme, the\n \nCentral Government \nhas \nalso\n \nbeen\n \n \nimplementing Market Intervention\n \nScheme (MIS) \n \nfor procurement \n \nof \n \nhorticultural\n \n \nContd…2/\n-\n \n\n-\n2\n-\n \n \n \ncommodities which are perishable in nature and are not covered under the Price \nSupport Scheme.  The objective of intervention is to protect the growers of these \ncommodities from making dist\nress sale in the event of a bumper crop during the peak \narrival period when the prices tend to fall below economic levels and cost of production.    \nThe Market Intervention Scheme (MIS) is i\nmplemented at the request of a S\ntate / UT \ngovernment which is read\ny to bear 50 percent of the loss (25 percent in case of North\n-\nEastern States), if any, i\nncurred on its implementation. \nThe extent of total amount of \nloss to be shared on a 50:50 basis between the central government and the state \ngovernment is restricted to\n \n25 percent of the total procurement value which includes \ncost of the commodity procured plus permitted overhead expenses.  Under the Scheme, \nin accordance with MIS guidelines, a pre\n-\ndetermined quantity at the fixed Market \nIntervention Price (MIP) is procu\nred by \nNational Agricultural Cooperative Marketing \nFederation (\nNAFED\n)\n \nas the Central agency and the agencies designated by the state \ngovernment for a fixed period or till the prices are stabilized above the MIP whichever is \nearlier.  The area of operation \nis restricted to the concerned state only.\n \n \n******\n \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|12|UNSTARRED |315", "t": "Development Boards", "head": "���������������������\n�������������������������������������������\n�������������������������������������������������