ing for urban poor and constructing housing units \nunder slums development programme is running as per schedule and \nif so, the details thereof; and if not, the reasons therefor;  \n \n(b)  the State-wise and city-wise number of housing units \nconstructed under the above schemes,  year-wise during the last \nthree years;  \n \n(c) whether the Government has received complaints in \nimplementation of above schemes in certain States; and  \n \n(d)  if so, the details thereof and the action taken/being taken by the \nGovernment in this regard?       \n                                          \n                                                ANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOUSING AND \nURBAN AFFAIRS \n \n(RAO INDERJIT SINGH) \n \n(a)  : Government has launched ‘Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana-\nHousing for All (Urban)’ Mission on 25.6.2015 to provide central \nassistance to States/UTs for prov iding housing to all eligible urban \npoor, including slum dwellers. T he mission envisages that houses \nconstructed by the States / UTs should have basic civic infrastructure \nlike water, sanitation, sewerage, road, electricity etc.  \nContd…2/- \n\n \n-2- \n \nThe PMAY (U) scheme guidelines require States/UTs to conduct \ndemand assessment and validate the same to arrive at the actual \ndemand for housing among its citizens belonging to the urban poor.  \n \n \n(b): State and City-w ise details of housing units constructed during \nthe last three years and the current year under PMAY(U) mission are \nat Annexure. \n \n(c) & (d) : Complaints received in connection with the \nimplementation of PMAY(U) mission are sent to State Government \n/Union Territories (UTs) for remedial action as the implementation of  \nprojects are undertaken by the respective State Governments/UTs \nand their implementing agencies, primarily Urban Local Bodies. \n \n ****** \n \n \n \n \n\nAnnexure referred in answer to LSUSQ No - 474 due for 19.07.2017 \nStates / UTs and City wise details of Houses sanctioned, and Constructed \nby urban poor beneficiaries during last three year and current year under \nPradhan Mantri Awas Yojana - PMAY(Urban) \n \nAs on 10th July 2017 \nMonitoring Division‐ MoHUA\n \n \n \n \nSr. No. \n \nCity Name State Name Houses \nSanctioned \nHouses \nCompleted \n1 Port Blair A&N Island 609 - \n  A&N Island Total  609 - \n2 Atmakur Andhra Pradesh 1,028 - \n3 Nellimarla Andhra Pradesh 325 170 \n4 Palasa Andhra Pradesh 192 100 \n5 Rajam Andhra Pradesh 1 1\n6 Amadalavalasa Andhra Pradesh 512 432 \n7 Srikakulam Andhra Pradesh 1,476 196 \n8 Parvathipuram Andhra Pradesh 836 23 \n9 Bobbili Andhra Pradesh 385 48 \n10 Salur Andhra Pradesh 588 12 \n11 Vizianagaram Andhra Pradesh 9,257 562 \n12 Visakhapatnam Andhra Pradesh 20,262 2,738\n13 Tuni Andhra Pradesh 5,100 29 \n14 Peddapuram Andhra Pradesh 1,724 - \n15 Rajahmundry Andhra Pradesh 4,214 14 \n16 Samalkota Andhra Pradesh 1,048 - \n17 Pithapuram Andhra Pradesh 874 - \n18 Kakinada Andhra Pradesh 4,620 12 \n19 Mandapeta Andhra Pradesh 4,064 - \n20 Ramachandrapuram Andhra Pradesh 1,090 2 \n21 Amalapuram Andhra Pradesh 1,636 - \n22 Tadepalligudem Andhra Pradesh 5,786 53 \n23 Eluru Andhra Pradesh 1,551 13 \n24 Bhimavaram Andhra Pradesh 9,501 1 \n25 Palacole Andhra Pradesh 7,470 52 \n26 Vijaywada Andhra Pradesh 11,443 49\n27 Gudivada Andhra Pradesh 3,317 5 \n28 Pedana Andhra Pradesh 1 1\n29 Machilipatnam Andhra Pradesh 1,851 253 \n30 Tadepalle Andhra Pradesh 1 1\n31 Mangalagiri Andhra Pradesh 2,592 - \n32 Sattenapalli Andhra Pradesh 642 2 \n33 Narasaraopet Andhra Pradesh 1,507 3 \n34 Chilakaluripet Andhra Pradesh 4,514 2 \n35 Guntur Andhra Pradesh 11,837 219 \n36 Tenali Andhra Pradesh 1,154 2 \n\nAnnexure referred in answer to LSUSQ No - 474 due for 19.07.2017 \nStates / UTs and City wise details of Houses sanctioned, and Constructed \nby urban poor beneficiaries during last three year and current year under \nPradhan Mantri Awas Yojana - PMAY(Urban) \n \nAs on 10th July 2017 \nMonitoring Division‐ MoHUA\n \n \n \n \nSr. No. \n \nCity Name State Name Houses \nSanctioned \nHouses \nCompleted \n37 Ponnur Andhra Pradesh 2,368 - \n38 Bapatla Andhra Pradesh 1 1\n39 Markapur Andhra Pradesh 1,020 - \n40 Chirala Andhra Pradesh 615 34 \n41 Ongole Andhra Pradesh 2,002 111 \n42 Kandukur Andhra Pradesh 1,438 1 \n43 Kavali Andhra Pradesh 4,512 131 \n44 Nellore Andhra Pradesh 10,052 248 \n45 Gudur Andhra Pradesh 5,106 3 \n46 Proddatur Andhra Pradesh 2,001 1 \n47 Kadapa Andhra Pradesh 4,337 156 \n48 Rayachoti Andhra Pradesh 640 54 \n49 Rajampet Andhra Pradesh 2 2\n50 Yemmiganur Andhra Pradesh 3,266 2 \n51 Kurnool Andhra Pradesh 10,013 13 \n52 Adoni Andhra Pradesh 4,711 7 \n53 Nandyal Andhra Pradesh 660 146 \n54 Rayadurg Andhra Pradesh 1,307 13 \n55 Guntakal Andhra Pra"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|12|UNSTARRED |475", "t": "List of Indian Workers Abroad", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.475 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 19.07.2017 \n \nLIST OF INDIAN WORKERS ABROAD \n \n475.  SHRI Y .V. SUBBA REDDY: \n \nWill the Minister of EXTERNAL AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether States are requesting the Ministry to maintain a list of \nIndians working in Gulf countries and distribute the same to \nStates concerned so that the concerned State can take \nnecessary steps whenever needed; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n \n(c) the reasons why Ministry cannot have bilateral agreement \nwith each of the Gulf countries so that prisoners can be sent \nback to respective States to execute remaining term of \npunishment in Indian jails; and  \n \n(d) the other suggestions received from other States in the \nconference conducted recently in Delhi by the Ministry and \nstatus of implementation of each of such suggestion?     \n \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n(SHRI M. J. AKBAR)  \n \n(a) & (b) Some States have inter -alia requested for sharing of \ndata of Indians working in Gulf countries from the concerned States  \nduring a recent conference held by Ministry of External Affairs with \nState Governments. This data is placed at Annexure . List of Indian s \nworking in Gulf countries from a specific State will be provided to \nthe concerned State Government separately.  \n \n(c) India has bilateral agreements on ‘Transfer of Sentenced \nPersons’ with several countries including Bahrain, Kuwait, Qatar, \nKingdom of Saudi Arabia and United Arab Emirates.   \n\n(d) Several suggestions were received during the Conference with \nState Governments by the Ministry. Some of the key suggestions \nwere: \n \n(i) Posting of language translators in Missions abroad; \n \n(ii) Early dispatch  of mortal remains of Indian workers from \noverseas; \n \n(iii) Pravasi Bhartiya Bima Yojna (PBBY) to be extended to \nEmigration Check Not Required (ECNR) passport holders \nalso; \n \n(iv) Taking stern action against illegal agents in different States; \n \n(v) Opening of more POE offices in U.P ., Bihar, Dehradun and \nNorth East States; \n \n(vi) Synchronization of Skill Development initiatives with \nOverseas Employment etc.  \n \nAction on these suggestions is under process.   \n \n***** \n  \n\nANNEXURE \n(3 pages) \n \nEmigration Clearance count for the year 2015 – State wise and country wise \nSTATE United \nArab \nEmirates \nSaudi                                 \nArabia \nKuwait Qatar Oman Bahrain TOTAL \nANDAMAN & NICOBAR 10 8 4 3 2 1 28 \nANDHRA PRADESH 12032 8875 15890 2611 4150 1017 44575 \nARUNACHAL PRADESH 5 4 1 2 1 1 14 \nASSAM 493 2915 622 99 110 21 4260 \nBIHAR 32538 42956 3955 10364 15300 1314 106427 \nCHANDIGARH 171 104 50 54 45 19 443 \nCHHATTISGARH 63 102 17 17 28 0 227 \nDADRA & NAGAR \nHAVELI 4 3 1 0 2 0 10 \nDAMAN & DIU 4 2 2 5 0 0 13 \nDELHI 635 1189 180 172 244 44 2464 \nGOA 279 195 544 47 87 30 1182 \nGUJARAT 2000 1369 538 902 1861 106 6776 \nHARYANA 852 678 236 244 168 48 2226 \nHIMACHAL PRADESH 393 274 122 236 120 15 1160 \nJAM