ER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS  \n(SHRI M. J. AKBAR) \n \n(a) Due to the strict provisions of privacy laws, the United States of \nAmerica, Canada, Australia and many countries in Europe do not share \ninformation about Indian nationals in their prisons. However, as per \ninformation available, 7448 Indian nationals are lodged in foreign jails in 81 \ncountries.  \n \n(b) & (c)  As soon as the information about detention/arrest o f an Indian \nnational is received by an Indian Mission/Post, it gets in touch with the \nlocal Foreign Office and other concerned local authorities to get consular \naccess to the detained/arrested Indian national to confirm his Indian \nnationality and ensure hi s/her welfare. Government of India provides legal \nassistance on means tested basis to deserving Indian nationals, including \nprisoners.  Government also provides help, advice and guidance ensuring \nfair and humane treatment in foreign jails, repatriation to India of those \nwho are released  and issues emergency certificates . In some countries, \nour Missions also request the local government s for grant of amnesty to \nthe arrested Indians and if any mercy petition for remission of sentences is \nreceived from the fam ily members of the Indian prisoners, the concerned \nMission forwards them to the local authorities for consideration.   A list \nshowing country -wise details of the Indian prisoners is attached at  the \nAnnexure. \n***** \n\nANNEXURE \n \nIndian Prisoners Abroad \n \nSl. No. Name of Country Number of \nprisoners \nSl. \nNo. Name of Country Number of \nprisoners \n1.  Armenia 1 42 Malaysia 304 \n2.  Austria 10 43 Maldives 11 \n3.  Australia   50 44 Mauritius 7 \n4.  Azerbaijan 1 45 Mexico 2 \n5.  Bahrain 68 46 Mozambique 5 \n6.  Bangladesh 126 47 Myanmar 38 \n7.  Belgium 25 48 Nepal 852 \n8.  Bhutan 53 49 Netherlands 1 \n9.  Brunei Darussalam  1 50 New Zealand 13 \n10.  Cambodia 5 51 Niger 1 \n11.  Canada  25 52 Nigeria 14 \n12.  China 225 53 Oman 101 \n13.  Colombia 5 54 Pakistan 468 \n14.  Cote D’ Ivoire 1 55 Panama 2 \n15.  Croatia 1 56 Peru 1 \n16.  Cuba 2 57 Philippines 10 \n17.  Cyprus 3 58 Portugal 3 \n18.  Denmark 8 59 Qatar 160 \n19.  Egypt 3 60 Romania 2 \n20.  Ethiopia  2 61 Russian Federation 4 \n21.  Djibouti 1 62 Saudi Arabia 2046 \n22.  Fiji 2 63 Senegal 1 \n23.  France 13 64 Seychelles 2 \n24.  Germany 54 65 Singapore 133 \n25.  Ghana 3 66 Slovak Republic 1 \n26.  Greece 17 67 South Africa 7 \n27.  Guatemala 4 68 Spain 21 \n28.  Indonesia 20 69 Sri Lanka 143 \n29.  Iran 28 70 Suriname 2 \n30.  Iraq 11 71 Thailand 48 \n31.  Ireland 3 72 Trinidad & Tobago 1 \n32.  Israel 4 73 Turkey 2 \n33.  Italy 80 74 Uganda 1 \n34.  Japan 1 75 United Arab Emirates 1376 \n35.  Jordan 1 76 Ukraine 1 \n36.  Kenya 2 77 U.S.A 281 \n37.  Korea (Republic of) 4 78 Uzbekistan 1 \n38.  Kuwait 506 79 Vietnam 1 \n39.  Kyrgyzstan 1 80 Yemen 1 \n40.  Lebanon 7 81 Zambia 1 \n41.  Libya 2    \n    Total 7448 \n \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|12|UNSTARRED |624", "t": "Revival of Tezpur Railway Station", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 624 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 19.07.2017 \n \nREVIVAL OF TEZPUR RAILWAY STATION \n \n624. SHRI RAM PRASAD SARMAH: \n \n  Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n(a)  whether it is a fact that a number of petitions have been received by his \nMinistry for revival of Tezpur (old) Railway Station under NF Railway in \nAssam and if so, the details thereof; \n(b)  whether it is also a fact that newly constructed Dekargaon Railway  \nstation is quite far from Tezpur town and passengers are facing problem \nto catch the trains; and \n(c) if so, the action taken by the Ministry to meet the demand of \npassengers? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n(SHRI RAJEN GOHAIN) \n(a): Y es, Madam. A few representations have been received including a \nreference from Chief Minister, Assam on the revival of Tezpur (old) station. \n(b): Dekargaon railway station is located at a distance of about 7 Km from \nTezpur town. \n(c):  Dekargaon -Tezpur town, part of the Meter Gauge track, was not \nconverted to Broad Gauge at the request of the then Assam Government. \nReconnection of Tezpur town to Dekargaon has been mooted subsequently. \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|12|UNSTARRED |625", "t": "Misleading Advertisement on PMAY", "head": "O.I.H \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 625 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON JULY 19, 2017 \n \nMISLEADING ADVERTISEMENT ON PMAY \n \nNo. 625 \n  \nSHRI  PANKAJ CHAUDHARY: \nSHRI PRAHLAD SINGH PATEL: \n \nWill the Minister of HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Pradhan Mantri Aawas Yo jana (PMAY) Urban is being run in the \ncountry and if so, the details thereof; \n(b) the target set regarding the number of families to be  provided houses during \nthe financial year 2017-18, State-wise; \n(c) whether the scheme is likely to  be implemented through Government \nagencies or the builders from the private sector and if  so,  the  details  thereof,  \nState-wise including Madhya Pradesh; \n(d) whether the Government is aware that several private builders are looting the \ncommon  man  by  using  Pradhan  Mantri Aawas  Yojana  in  their  advertisements \nopenly; \n(e)  if so,  whether  the  Government proposes to take  any  action against such \nbuilders who  publish  misleading advertisements; and \n(f)  the  details  of  t he  amount sanctioned under PMAY  Housing for All (urban)  \nduring  the  last  3  years  and  the current year, State-wise? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \n(RAO INDERJIT SINGH) \n**** \n(a): In pursuance of the Government’s vision of facilitating housing for all by 2022, \nPradhan Mantri Awas Yojana (Urban) {PMAY(U)} was  launched on 25th June 2015 \nfor providing houses to all eligible families/beneficiaries by 2022. \n \nSo far a total of 4884 projects have been considered for providing central \nassistance of Rs. 32,860.16 Cr for construction of 21, 00,859 houses under \nPMAY(U). \nContd….2/- \n\n(b): Under PMAY(U), target of Govern ment is to provide admissible central \nassistance for all housing requirement as may be proposed by States/UTs during \nthe Mission period to achieve the goal of ‘Housing for All by 2022’. \n \n(c ): Private sector participation is envisaged under the A ffordable Housing in \nPartnership (AHP) and In-situ Slum R edevelopment (ISSR) components of the \nPMAY (U) mission. Central assistance of  Rs.1 lakh per house, on an average, \nunder the ISSR component and Rs.1.5  lakh per house under AHP component, is \nadmissible for projects appr oved under the mission.  St ate/UT wise details of \nhouses sanctioned/central assistance invo lved under PMAY(U ) including ISSR \nand AHP components is at Annexure-I. \n \n(d) & (e):  To deal with alleged com plaints/representations regarding bogus \nbuilders/developers who have register ed and enlisted a large number of \ncustomers for allotment of economically  weaker sections/lower income group \nhouses in the name of Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana (Urban)  {PMAY(U)}, the \nfollowing actions have been taken by the Ministry: \n \n(i) To ensure transparency and facilitate the citizens  in registration for \ndemand assessment, the Ministry has  enabled the facility of online \napplication using the platform of  Common Service Centre(CSC) and \nPMAY(U) MIS Portal.` \n \n(ii) A disclaimer has been posted on the website of the Ministry intimating \ngeneral public that this Ministry has not authorized any private entity or \nperson to collect money as a consideration for availing of any benefit under \nthe PMAY (U) Mission.  \n \n(iii) State/UT Governments have been r equested to issue disclaimer/public \nnotice cautioning the general public about unscrupulous individuals/ \nentities from cheating the general public.  \n \n(iv) Principal Secretaries/ Secretarie s in charge of Housing/ Urban \nDevelopment have been requested to exercise vigil on such \nadvertisements or instances where the nomenclature of PMAY (U) mission \nis being used with mala fide int entions and to proceed against the \nwrongdoers as per law.  The States/ UTs have further been advised to issue \nappropriate instructions to the concerned officials at the district/ULB level \nfor similar action at their end. \n….3/- \n\n-3- \n \n(v) A public notice cautioning general public against possible fraud in the \nname of PMAY(U) (coloured adve rtisement) has been published on \n14\nth  May, 2017 in 51 major regional dailies (pan India) through DAVP. \n \n(f):  The  details  of  the  amount s anctioned under PMAY Housing for All (urban)  \nduring  the  last  3  years  and  the current year, State-wise is at Annexure-I. \n \n                                                          ….. \n\n1 A&N Island (UT)                         -                        609                         -                       9.14 \n2 Andhra Pradesh               195,047                        27                   6,426              2,944.35 \n3 Arunanchal Pradesh                   1,606                         -                            1                   78.44 \n4 Assam                 24,355                   2,443                        69                 402.16 \n5 Bihar                 88,293                        24                   2,654        "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|12|UNSTARRED |626", "t": "Launch of GSAT-17", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \n DEPARTMENT OF SPACE \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.626 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON WEDNESDAY, JULY 19, 2017 \nLAUNCH OF GSAT-17 \n626.  SHRI C. MAHENDRAN: \nSHRI R. PARTHIPAN: \nWill the PRIME MINISTER be pleased to state: \n(a)  whether the  Government  has  successfully  launched GSAT-17 \ncommunication satellite onboard the  Ariane-5 launch vehicle \nrecently; \n(b)  if so, the details thereof; \n(c)  whether the satellite will be an  addition to the Indian \ncommunication satellites that are already providing services; \n(d) if so, the details thereof; and \n(e) whether the satellite will provide  meteorological and satellite -\nbased data to  help rescue services and if so, the details  \nthereof? \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF PERSONNEL, PG & \nPENSIONS AND IN THE PRIME MINISTER’S OFFICE \n(DR. JITENDRA SINGH): \n(a) Yes, Madam. \n\n(b) GSAT-17 communication satellite, with a lift -off mass of      \n3477 Kg, carrying communication, Data Relay Transponder \n(DRT), Search & Rescue Payload was  successfully launched on \nJune 29, 2017 using Ariane -5 launch vehicle from Kourou \nlaunch base of Arianespace. \n(c) Yes Madam. \n(d) GSAT-17 is presently undergoing in-orbit tests. Subsequently, it \nwill be inducted into the INSAT/GSAT system for providing \nvarious communication services to the country in C,   \nExtended-C and S-band. \n(e) GSAT-17 carries a Data Relay Transponder for receiving \nmeteorological, hydrological and oceanographic data from \nAutomatic Weather Stations, Automatic Rain Gauges and Agro \nMet Stations and relaying back for down linking in extended   \nC-Band. It also carries a Search & Rescue Payload, which picks \nup and relays the alert signals originating from the distress \nbeacons of maritime, aviation and land based users to help in \nrescue services. \n***** \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|12|UNSTARRED |627", "t": "BIMSTEC Security Chiefs’ Meet", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS  \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.627 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 19.07.2017 \n \nBIMSTEC SECURITY CHIEFS’ MEET \n \n627. SHRI B.N. CHANDRAPPA: \n SHRI NALIN KUMAR KATEEL: \n \nWill the Minister of EXTERNAL AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether India hosted the meeting of the National Security Chiefs \nof BIMSTEC Member States recently; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n \n(c) the details of issues discussed during the meeting of the BIMSTEC \nMember States; \n \n(d) whether the meeting of the BIMSTEC Members States has entered \ninto any agreement to counter common security threats such as \nterrorism and extremism; and \n \n(e) if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n(SHRI M. J. AKBAR) \n \n(a) & (b) Yes.  The  first meeting  of  National  Security  Chiefs  of  \nBIMSTEC Member States was hosted by India in New Delhi on 21 March \n2017.  \n \n(c) The meeting discussed ways of addressing traditional and non -\ntraditional security challenges and working out collective strategies to \ndeal with spread of terrorism, violent extremist and radicalization. The \nmeeting also discussed cooperation in cyber security; maritime security, \nincluding humanitarian assistance and disaster relief;  use of emerging \nspace technologies fo r addressing security challenges ; a proposal for \nsetting up of a BIMSTEC Himalayan Science Council to study the health \nof the ecological systems and their impact on human security ; and \ncapacity building. \n \n(d) & (e) The meeting agreed , inter-alia, to deepen cooperation \namong respective cyber inst itutions through a Joint F orum on cyber \nsecurity; and to establish a track 1.5 BIMSTEC Security Dialogue Forum.  \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|12|UNSTARRED |628", "t": "Training in Agricultural and Allied Sectors", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP\n \n \nLOK\n \nSABHA\n \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.\n \n628\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON \n19.07\n.2017\n \n \nTRAINING IN AGRICULTURAL AND ALLIED SECTORS\n \n \n†628\n.\n \nPROF. CHINTAMANI MALVIYA:\n \n \nDR. RAVINDRA KUMAR RAY:\n \nSHRI SHER \nSINGH GHUBAYA:\n \n \nWill the Minister of SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP be \npleased to state\n:\n \n \n(\na)  \n \nthe  details  of  the  schemes/ programmes being run by the Government for skill \ndevelopment and training in Agricultural and allied sectors for the \nfarmers in the country;\n \n \n(b)\n \n \nthe number of farmers imparted training through these schemes along with the \nbenefit accrued to them;\n \n \n(c) \n \nwhether the Government has earmarked any fund for this purpose under various \nschemes, State\n-\nwise including Jharkhand; \nand\n \n \n(d) \n \nif so, the details of the funds earmarked and spent for this purpose during each of the \nlast three years and the current year?\n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) IN THE MINISTRY OF\n \nSKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP\n \n(SHRI RAJIV \nPRATAP RUDY)\n \n \n(a) &\n \n(b)\n \nGovernment of India is implementing two flagship schemes known as Pradhan \nMantri Kaushal Vikas Yojana (PMKVY) and Pradhan Mant\nri Kaushal Kendra (PMKK) on \npan\n–\nIndia basis to cover the prospective youths including farmers.  PMKVY enables large \nnumber of prospective youths for taking \nS\nhort \nT\nerm \nT\nraining\n \n(STT)\n \nand Recognition of Prior \nLearning (RPL) through accredited and affiliated training partner/training cente\nrs. \nThis \nscheme has two components namely Centrally Sponsored Centrally Managed (CSCM) and \nCentrally Sponsored State Managed (CSSM). \nUnder\n \nCSCM\n, \nskill development training is \nimparted across 221 job roles\n \ncovering 35 sectors including a\ngriculture. Out of 2\n21 job roles, \n10 job roles \nnamely\n;\n \nAnimal Health Worker,\n \nAquaculture worker, Green House Operator,\n \nDairy Farmer/ Entrepreneur, Tractor operator, Gardener, Micro Irrigation Technician, Organic \ngrower, Quality Seed Grower and Small poultry farmer \nrelate\n \nto a\ngriculture sector\n.\n \nUnder \nCSCM component of PMKVY, as on 6th July 2017, total 30,67,080 candidates are trained / \nundergoing training across country. Out of them, \n2,27,947 \ncandidates \nincluding farmer \nare \ntrained \n/ undergoing training \nin a\ngriculture sector.\n \n \nU\nnder \nCSSM component known as \nstate engagement component \nof PMKVY, there \nare\n \nprovision\ns\n \nfor flexibilit\ny\n \nto \nState\ns government \nto identify additional job roles as per the \nlocal needs. \nUnder this component, the \ntarget of training \n57\n,\n670 \ncandidates has been \nallocated in the State of \nJharkhand\n \nfor four years (2016\n-\n20) under State Engagement \nComponent of PMKVY.\n \n \n \nUnder the PMKK, Ministry intends to establish a model aspirational skill centres in \nevery district for imparting skill training th\nrough PMKVY. PMKKs have been allocated to all \nthe 24 districts of Jharkhand.\n \n \n(c)\n \n&\n \n(d)\n \n \n \n \n \n \nPMKVY 2015\n-\n16 has been approved with an outlay of Rs. 1500 Cr and modified \nPMKVY has been approved by the Union Cabinet with an outlay of Rs.12000 crore to impart \nskilling to one crore people over four years (2016\n-\n2020). \nUnder CSSM, \n25% of total \nfunds \nand correspondingly physical targets have been allocated to States/UTs including Jharkhand. \nDetails of funds allocated under State \n–\nengagement component of PMKVY 2016\n-\n20 is at \nAnnexure\n-\nI\n.\n \n\nAnnexure\n-\nI\n \n \nStates/UTs\n-\nwise details \nof Physical targets and Funds allocated under State \nengagement component of PMKVY 2016\n-\n20:\n \n \nS. No.\n \nStates/UTs\n \nPhysical targets \nallocated to \nStates/UTs\n \nTotal funds \nallocated to \nStates/UTs (in Cr.)\n \n1\n.\n \n \nJAMMU & KASHMIR\n \n47302\n \n69.36\n \n2\n.\n \n \nHIMACHAL PRADESH\n \n49499\n \n72.59\n \n3\n.\n \n \nPUNJAB\n \n55029\n \n80.69\n \n4\n.\n \n \nUTTARAKHAND\n \n48238\n \n70.74\n \n5\n.\n \n \nHARYANA\n \n56038\n \n82.17\n \n6\n.\n \n \nRAJASTHAN\n \n64526\n \n94.62\n \n7\n.\n \n \nUTTAR PRADESH\n \n142550\n \n209.04\n \n8\n.\n \n \nBIHAR\n \n89665\n \n131.49\n \n9\n.\n \n \nSIKKIM\n \n34348\n \n50.37\n \n10\n.\n \n \nARUNACHAL PRADESH\n \n29510\n \n43.27\n \n11\n.\n \n \nNAGALAND\n \n33021\n \n48.42\n \n12\n.\n \n \nMANIPUR\n \n32472\n \n47.62\n \n13\n.\n \n \nMIZORAM\n \n36671\n \n53.77\n \n14\n.\n \n \nTRIPURA\n \n37062\n \n54.35\n \n15\n.\n \n \nMEGHALAYA\n \n33642\n \n49.33\n \n16\n.\n \n \nASSAM\n \n47258\n \n69.30\n \n17\n.\n \n \nWEST BENGAL\n \n123550\n \n181.17\n \n18\n.\n \n \nJHARKHAND\n \n57670\n \n84.57\n \n19\n.\n \n \nODISHA\n \n58046\n \n85.12\n \n20\n.\n \n \nCHHATTISGARH\n \n48532\n \n71.17\n \n21\n.\n \n \nMADHYA PRADESH\n \n84058\n \n123.26\n \n22\n.\n \n \nGUJARAT\n \n77825\n \n114.12\n \n23\n.\n \n \nMAHARASHTRA\n \n167127\n \n245.07\n \n24\n.\n \n \nANDHRA PRADESH\n \n64610\n \n94.74\n \n25\n.\n \n \nKARNATAKA\n \n94164\n \n138.08\n \n26\n.\n \n \nGOA\n \n46951\n \n68.85\n \n27\n.\n \n \nKERALA\n \n71456\n \n104.78\n \n28\n.\n \n \nTAMIL NADU\n \n140881\n \n206.59\n \n29\n.\n \n \nTELANGANA\n \n59611\n \n87.41\n \n30\n.\n \n \nDELHI\n \n81657\n \n119.74\n \n31\n.\n \n \nANDAMAN NICOBAR\n \n4108\n \n6.02\n \n32\n.\n \n \nCHANDIGARH\n \n10288\n \n15.09\n \n33\n.\n \n \nDADAR & NAGAR HAVELI\n \n4000\n \n5.87\n \n34\n.\n \n \nLAKSHADWEEP\n \n4018\n \n5.89\n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|12|UNSTARRED |629", "t": "National Urban Sanitation Policy", "head": "Contd…..2 \nO.I.H. \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 629 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON JULY 19, 2017 \n \nNATIONAL URBAN SANITATION POLICY \n \nNo. 629  SHRI PASHUPATI NATH SINGH:  \n \nWill the Minister of HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether Dhanbad district of Jharkhand is one of the most polluted districts in \nthe country;  \n \n(b) if so, the details of the schemes started, fund allocated and the target set \nunder National Urban Sanitation Policy, St ate-wise including in Dhanbad district \nof Jharkhand during the last three years;  \n \n(c) whether the Government has ascertained the reasons for not getting the \ntargets achieved under the National Ur ban Sanitation Policy in Dhanbad district \nof Jharkhand so far; and  \n \n(d) if so, the reasons therefor and the time by which the work is likely to be \ncompleted? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \n \n(RAO INDERJIT SINGH) \n \n(a): As per Swachh Survekshan 2017 conducted by the Ministry of Housing and \nUrban Affairs under Swachh Bharat Mission (Urban), Dhanbad city is placed at \nranking of 109 out of 434 cities. \n \n(b): National Urban Sanitation Policy (NUSP) was approved by the Government \nof India in the year 2008 with overall goal to transform urban India into \ncommunity-driven, totally sanitized, healthy and liveable cities and towns. \nSwachh Bharat Mission (Urban) and Atal Mission for Rejuvenation and Urban \n\n-2- \n \n \n \nTransformation (AMRUT) launched by the Govt. of India target to achieve goal of \nNUSP with more emphasis on totally sanitized cities and towns. The funds \nrelease status under SBM (Urban) during last three years and allocation of \nAdditional Central Assistance (ACA) under AMRUT are at Annexure-I and \nAnnexure-II respectively. \n \n(c) & (d): Swachh Bharat Mission (Urban), being implemented in  4041 statutory \ntowns, aims to make these towns 100% Open Defecation Free with 100% \nscientific management of municipal solid waste in these cities by 2\nnd October, \n2019. The components of the Mission are Individual Household Latrines (IHHL), \nCommunity Toiles (CT), Public Toilets (PT), Urinals, Solid Waste Management \n(SWM), IEC & PA (Information, Educati on, Communication & Public Awareness) \nand CB & A&OE (Capacity Building and Administrative & Office Expense). AMRUT \nScheme is being implemented in 500 cities/towns having population of more than \none lakh during Financial Year 2015-16 to Financial Year 2019-20. The major \ncomponents under AMRUT are water supply, sewerage and septage \nmanagement, storm water drainage, urban transport, capacity building, reform \nimplementation and development of green spaces and parks to make the \ncities/towns more liveable. \n \n In Dhanbad, 27,611 IHHLs have been constructed and 24,981 IHHLs are \nunder construction. Besides this 43 Community toilets with 200 seats and 50 \nModular toilets with 100 seats have already been constructed and the under \nconstruction Community toilets are 20 Nos. with 200 seats and 2 Community \nToilets-cum-Skill development centre with 24 seats. For Solid Waste \nManagement, tenders were called for establishment of the processing plant and \nthe tenders received are under consideration which will be finalised soon. \n \n  Till now 14 cities in Jharkhand have been declared as Open Defecation \nFree (ODF) and by 2\nnd October, 2017 all cities of Jharkhand including Dhanbad \nwill become ODF. \n \n****** \n\n-3- \n \n \n \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (B) OF LOK SABHA UNSTARRED \nQUESTION NO.629 FOR 19.07.2017 REGARDING NATIONAL URBAN SANITATION \nPOLICY \nANNEXURE-I \n \nFund release status under Swachh Bharat Mission (Urban) during last three year \n(Rs. in crore) \nSl.  State/UT 2014-15 2015-16 2016-17 Total \n1 A&N Islands  0.1379 0.2781 0.4160\n2 Andhra Pradesh 40.0000 73.1850 204.1050 317.2900\n3 Arunachal Pradesh 9.3600 1.2104 5.7261 16.2965\n4 Assam 0.2300  14.4313 14.6613\n5 Bihar 37.7200 20.0000 112.7030 170.4230\n6 Chandigarh  1.7000 2.7151 4.4151\n7 Chhattisgarh 30.7900 35.8715 84.7674 151.4289\n8 Dadra & Nagar Haveli  0.1618   0.1618\n9 Daman & Diu  0.1957   0.1957\n10 Delhi 7.5300 97.2200   104.7500\n11 Goa 3.1700 3.0466 2.0800 8.2966\n12 Gujarat 57.2986 106.6076 240.2098 404.1160\n13 Haryana 17.9200 11.6476 45.0850 74.6526\n14 Himachal Pradesh 6.0200 0.9000 9.9522 16.8722\n15 Jammu & Kashmir 14.7500 4.5700 20.3019 39.6219\n16 Jharkhand 15.2700 23.9619 98.1925 137.4244\n17 Karnataka 80.0100 70.0000 18.1150 168.1250\n18 Kerala 19.1800 14.9900 9.4500 43.6200\n19 Madhya Pradesh 21.0258 135.8042 270.6654 427.4954\n20 Maharashtra 135.0000 87.0300 95.0600 317.0900\n21 Manipur 11.2100 1.6450 2.4722 15.3272\n22 Meghalaya 4.0500    4.0500\n23 Mizoram 9.7900 1.0700   10.8600\n24 Nagaland 10.5200 3.2030 0.9900 14.7130\n25 Odisha 1.4300 24.6132 79.0341 105.0773\n26 Puducherry 1.9530  9.5220 11.4750\n27 Punjab 41.4000 15.0000 10.4600 66.8600\n28 Rajasthan 60.7300 45.0000 303.6876 409.4176\n29 Sikkim 3.0856 0.3796 0.4787 "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|12|UNSTARRED |63", "t": "Expansion of Bharat-Oman Refineries", "head": " \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 63 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 17th JULY, 2017 \n \nEXPANSION OF BHARAT-OMAN REFINERIES \n \n63: SHRI LAXMI NARAYAN YADAV: \n \nपैट्रो ल ियम और प्राकृ तिक गैस मंत्री \nWill the Minister of PETROLEUM AND NATURAL GAS be pleased to state: \n(a) whether any expansion work has been undertaken in the Bharat -Oman \nRefineries Limited during the last three years;  \n(b) if so, the details thereof; and  \n(c) the present status of the said expansion work? \n \nANSWER \nपैट्रोलियम और प्राक ृ लिक गैस मंत्रािय में राज्य मंत्री (स्विंत्र प्रभार) (श्री धमेन्द्र प्रधान) \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF PETROLEUM AND NATURAL GAS (SHRI \nDHARMENDRA PRADHAN) \n(a) to (c): BPCL has reported that Bharat -Oman Refineries Limited (BOR L) has \nundertaken a debottlenecking project to increase the refinery processing capacity \nfrom 6 to 7.8 Million Metric Tonne Per Annum (MMTPA) and also to meet the BS -VI \nproduct specifications. The estimated cost of the project is Rs. 3072 crores. The \nmechanical completion is scheduled for September 2018. As on June 15, 2017 \noverall cumulative physical progress of the project stands at 48%. \n \n \n************ "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|12|UNSTARRED |630", "t": "PMs Programme ‘Mann Ki Baat’", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF INFORMATION AND BROADCASTING \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 630 \n( TO BE ANSWERED ON 19.07.2017 ) \n \nPMs PROGRAMME  ‘MANN KI BAAT’  \n   \n630. SHRI R.P. MARUTHARAJAA: \nWill the Minister of INFORMATION AND BROADCASTING  \nbe pleased to state: \n(a) whether the Government is implementing the Prime Minister ’s programme \n‘Mann Ki Baat’; \n(b) if so, the number of Broadcasts made in Regional Languages in various radio \nstations in the country; \n(c)  the commercial income of Akashwani during the last two years, yearwise;  \n(d) whether the Government has any data on the number of countries in which the \nprogramme was broadcast and listened to and if so, the details thereof; and  \n(e) whether the Government provides option of any marketing companies and if \nso, the details thereof ? \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE  MINISTRY OF INFORMATION AND \nBROADCASTING (COL RAJYAVARDHAN RATHORE (Retd.) \n \n(a): Prasar Bharati has informed that All India Radio is regularly broadcasting \nPrime Minister’s  programme ‘Mann Ki Baat’. \n(b): The regional versions of the Prime Minister’s ‘Mann Ki Baat’ are originated by \nthe non-Hindi capital AIR Stations immediately after the completion of the original \nbroadcast of ‘Mann Ki Baat’ on the same day in 18 languages and 33 dialects and \nthese are relayed by all AIR stations including Local Radio Stations in their \nrespective regional languages.  The repeat broadcast of the Regional Language \nVersions on respective Regional networks, takes place at 8.00 p.m on the same \nday of the broadcast.  The English and Sanskrit versions of this broadcast is also \ncarried by AIR, Delhi. \n (c) : Revenue earned from ‘Mann Ki Baat’ programme for the last two years; \n \nYears Revenue Earned \n(in Rupees) \n2015-16 Rs. 4,78,22,480/- \n2016-17 Rs. 5,19,00,000/- \n \n(d):  ‘Mann Ki Baat’ is disseminated on transmitters for domestic audience and \nthrough internet and shortwave (SW) transmitters for global listeners. \n(e):  No, Madam. \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|12|UNSTARRED |631", "t": "Cloud Computing", "head": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS  \nDEPARTMENT OF TELECOMMUNICATIONS  \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.631 \n TO BE ANSWERED ON 19th JULY, 2017 \n \nCLOUD COMPUTING \n \n631. SHRI KESINENI NANI: \n \nWill the Minister of COMMUNICATIONS be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether the Government proposes to create a new regulatory framework for \nsecuring cloud computing;  \n \n(b)  if so, the details thereof;  \n \n(c)  the major recommendations of TRAI’s consultation paper on the same; and  \n \n(d)  whether the Government has accepted the said recommendations of the TRAI \nand if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (IC) OF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS & \n MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n \n \n(a) &  (b) Department of Telecommunications (DoT) has sought the \nrecommendations from Telecom Regulatory Authority of India (TRAI) on cloud \nbased services in the country covering various aspects like security, privacy, \nQuality of Service ( QoS), legal framework involving multiple jurisdictions across \ninternational boundary etc.  \n \n(c) & (d)  TRAI has issued a Consultation Paper on ‘ Cloud Computing’ dated \n10-06-2016. TRAI is yet to submit its recommendations to the Government. \n \n \n********** \n \n \n \n \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|12|UNSTARRED |632", "t": "Achievements of ISRO Programme", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \n DEPARTMENT OF SPACE \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.632 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON WEDNESDAY, JULY 19, 2017 \nACHIEVEMENTS OF ISRO PROGRAMME \n632.  SHRI RAJU SHETTY: \nWill the PRIME MINISTER be pleased to state: \n(a)  whether the country’s space  programme is moving in positive \ndirection; \n(b)  if so, the details of this recent  achievements of the \nprogrammes in brief; \n(c)  whether any activities are proposed  to be taken up shortly \nbased on the experience gained in recent achievements; and \n(d)  if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor? \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF PERSONNEL, PG & \nPENSIONS AND IN THE PRIME MINISTER’S OFFICE \n(DR. JITENDRA SINGH): \n(a) & (b) \nYes, Madam. Indian space programme  is striving to provide \nincreased space based capability and witnessed significant \nachievements in recent times. Some of the notable \nachievements include- \n\n(i) Operationalisation of GSLV -MkII with home -grown \nCryogenic Upper Stage (CUS) with indigenous capability \nfor launching 2-tonne class satellites. \n(ii) Successful launch of first developmental flight of GSLV -\nMkIII, which validated new version of Indigenous \nCryogenic Engine. With this capability,  it will be possible \nto launch up to 4 -tonne class of communication satellites \ninto Geosynchronous Transfer Orbits (GTO). \n(iii) Realisation of South Asia Satellite to enable South Asian \ncountries to establish SATCOM based services su ch        \nas Television/DTH, VSAT, e-governance, banking ,              \ntele-medicine & tele -education etc., with coverage over \nSouth Asia. \n(iv) Launch of 104 Satellites in a single PSLV (PSLV -C37) \nmission– Maximum satellites launched in a single launch \nmission till date. \n(v) Realisation of 7-satellite NavIC ( Navigation – Indian \nConstellation) to provide Position, Navigation and Timing \nServices. \n(vi) Augmentation of Satellite Communication with high -\nthroughput communication satellites. \n(vii) Successful flight testing of Technology Demonstrators of \nRe-usable Launch Vehicle (RLV -TD) and Scramjet           \nAir-breathing Engine. \n\n(viii) INSAT-3D & 3DR together are providing meteorological \ndata every 15 minutes for enabling weather forecasting. \nOcean surface wind vector data from SCATSAT -1 are \nbeing used operationally by global user community.  \n(ix) Augmentation of earth observation capability with High \nResolution Cartographic and Resource monitoring \nsatellites. \n(x) Placing a unique multi -wavelength observatory placed in \norbit, carrying instruments realis ed through Indian \nacademic institutes to enhance understanding of universe \nand astronomical phenomena. \n(xi) Enabling host of applications using synergy of earth \nobservation, communication and navigation satellites in \ngovernance and development. \n(c) & (d) \nBased on the experience gained,  various activities are planned \nin the near future, which include: \n(i) Second Developmental flight of GSLV -Mk III with \nindigenously developed high thrust cryogenic engine and \nstage in first half of 2018.  \n(ii) Realisation of High throughput Communication ‘GSAT -11’, \ncarrying Ku & Ka Band communication payloads with \nmultiple spot beams, capable of providing up to 10 Gbps \nthroughput. \n\n(iii) Launch of Chandrayaan -2 Mission India’s second Lunar \nmission, Chandrayaan -2 with indigenous L ander, Rover \nand Orbiter Modules during first half of 2018. \n(iv) Augmentation of Indigenous navigation services.  \n(v) Launch of high resolution cartographic satellite for large \nscale mapping applications, which include infrastructure \nplanning, urban & rural development, utility management, \nnatural resources inventory & management, disaster \nmanagement.    \n***** \n \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|12|UNSTARRED |633", "t": "NSSO Report on Swachhata Status", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF STATISTICS AND PROGRAMME IMPLEMENTATION \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 633 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON WEDNESDAY, THE 19TH JULY, 2017 \n \nNSSO REPORT ON SWACHHATA STATUS \n \n633. SHRI SUMAN BALKA: \n \nWill the Minister of STATISTICS AND PRO GRAMME IMPLEMENTATION \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the NSSO has conducted any survey on swachhata status \nin the country; \n(b) if so, the details and the findings thereof; and \n(c) the reaction of the Government thereto? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER FOR STATISTICS AND PROGRAMM E IMPLEMENTATION [SHRI \nD.V. SADANANDA GOWDA] \n \n(a) and (b): Yes, Madam.  A Rapid Survey on Swachhta Status was \nconducted by the National Sample Survey Office (NSSO) during May -June \n2015.  The survey aimed to give a snapshot of the situation on the \navailability/accessibility of toilets, solid waste and liquid waste \nmanagement at sample village/ward and household levels. Some major \nfindings of the report are given below: \n \n• In rural areas, 45.3% households reported to have sanitary toilets. In \nthese households, the percentage of persons using \nhousehold/community toilet was 95.6%. \n• In urban areas, 88.8% households reported to have sanitary toilets. \nFor the households having sanitary toilet, the percentage of persons \nusing household/community/public toilet was 98.7% \n• In rural areas, 50.5% of the households kept the garbage at a \nspecified place outside their own house, 24.4% households disposed \nof the garbage in the nearby agriculture field, 5.5% households kept \n\nit at the common place outside the house, 4.4% households \ndisposed of the garbage in the biogas plant or manure pit whereas \n15.1% households threw it around the house. \n• In urban areas, 64.2% wards were found to have a dumping place for \nsolid waste. \n• 36.7% villages had pakkinali and 19.0% villages had katchinali  as \ndrainage arrangement for waste water coming out of the rural \nhouseholds. 44.4% villages had no drainage arrangement. \n• 56.4% wards reported to have sewer network for disposal of liquid \nwaste. \n \n(c) This is a status report and the Government has taken note of \nswachhta situation as brought out by this report. \n \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|12|UNSTARRED |634", "t": "Setting up of NPP under Civil Nuclear Agreement", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nDEPARTMENT OF ATOMIC ENERGY \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.634 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 19.07.2017 \n \nSETTING UP OF NPP UNDER CIVIL NUCLEAR AGREEMENT \n \n634. SHRIVISHNU DAYAL RAM: \n SHRI JANAK RAM: \n \nWill the PRIME MINISTER be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether any progress has been made in case of s etting up of nuclear power \nplants after India signing the civil nuclear agreem ent and if so, the details \nthereof; \n \n(b) the reasons for the delay, if any; \n \n(c) whether hurdles, if any, will be removed in a t ime bound manner; and \n \n(d) if so, the details in this regard? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR PERSONNEL, PUBLIC GRIEVAN CES & \nPENSIONS AND PRIME MINISTER’S OFFICE (Dr. JITENDRA SINGH): \n \n(a) Yes, Sir. Following the signing of internationa l agreements on civil nuclear \ncooperation, agreements have been concluded for set ting up of four units \nof 1000 MW each at Kudankulam (KKNPP 3&4 and KKNPP 5&6) in \ntechnical cooperation with Russian Federation. The construction of KKNPP \n3&4 has commenced. Discussions with ElectricitedeFrance  (EDF) of \nFrance, M/s Westinghouse Electric Company (WEC) of the USA to set up \nlarge capacity nuclear power reactors in the country have also commenced. \n \n(b) to (d) Negotiations with foreign technology par tners involve careful consideration   \nof  various legal, regulatory, technical and commer cial issues and take \ntime. \n \n****** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|12|UNSTARRED |635", "t": "Direct Trains to Capitals from Allahabad", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n  \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 635 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 19.07.2017 \n \nDIRECT TRAINS TO CAPITALS FROM ALLAHABAD \n \n† 635. SHRI SHYAMA CHARAN GUPTA: \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state the action \ntaken on my letters regarding introduction of direct trains from \nAllahabad district to the capitals of all the States in the country? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI RAJEN GOHAIN) \nRequests/representations for introduction of new trains are received \nfrom various quarters i.e. General public, public representatives, \nZonal Railways etc. and action as found feasible and justified is \ntaken from time to time.  India being a vast country, it is not always \nfeasible to provide direct connection from any place to the capitals \nof all the States.  Allahabad station is presently connected to most \nof the State capitals.   Introduction of additional train from \nAllahabad is operationally not feasibl e, at present. However, \nintroduction of new train is an ongoing process over Indian Railways \nand is done keeping in view the operational feasibility, traffic \ndemand, resource availability, competing demands etc. \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|12|UNSTARRED |636", "t": "Special Training Programmes", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP\n \n \nLOK\n \nSABHA\n \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.\n \n636\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON \n19.07\n.2017\n \n \nSPECIAL TRAINING PROGRAMMES\n \n \n†\n \n636. DR. RAMESH POKHRIYAL“NISHANK”\n:\n \n \nWill the Minister of SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP \nbe pleased to state\n:\n \n \n(a) \n \nwhether the Ministry has started any special  training programme for \nadventure tourism, Eco\n-\ntourism, Organic farming, Food processing, Horticulture \nHerbal production and\n \nprocessing in Himalayan regions;\n \n \n(b)\n \n \nif so, the details thereof;\n \n \n(c) \n \nthe number of trainees out of the above who got employment after training;\n \n \n(d) \n \nthe goals set by the Government for the next three years; and\n \n \n(e) \n \nwhether\n \nany mechanism has been put in place by the Ministry to coordinate \nwith other ministries and the private sector and if so, the details thereof?\n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) IN THE MINISTRY OF\n \nSKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP\n \n(SHRI \nRAJIV PRATAP RUDY)\n \n \n(a) \nto (c\n)\n \nMinistry has not started any \nspecial  training programme for adventure \ntourism, Eco\n-\ntourism, Organic farming, Food processing, Horticulture Herbal \nproduction and processing in Himalayan regions. However, \nPradhan Mantri Kaushal \nVikas Yojana (PMKVY) \nis being implemented by National Skill Development \nCorporation for providing skill training to the \nprospective youth.\n \n \n \nThis scheme has two components known as Centrally Sponsored Centrally \nManaged (CSCM) and Cen\ntrally Sponsored State Managed (CSSM). Under CSCM, \nskill development training is imparted \nin 35 sectors \nacross 221 job roles \nincluding\n \nOrganic grower, Quality Seed Grower, Dairy Farmer/ Entrepreneur, Jam Jelly & \nKetchup Processing Technician, Handloom Weav\ner (Carpets), Tour Guide, Travel \nConsultant etc.\n \nUnder CSSM component known as state engagement component of \nPMKVY, there is a provisi\non for flexibilities to States G\novernment to identify additional \njob roles as per the local needs.\n \n \nUnder PMKVY, as on 6th\n \nJuly 2017, total 30,67,080 candidates are trained / \nundergoing training across various sectors including agriculture, tourism and \nprocession throughout the country. \n \n \n(d)\n \nMinistry is implementing PMKVY to train one crore youth for 4 years (2016\n-\n2020) with\n \na total outlay of Rs 12,000 crores.\n \n \n(e)\n \nThe Government of India has launched the National Labour Market Information \nSystem (LMIS) on the 15th July 2016 with a aim to serve a single window access \npoint for all skill development related data in the country\n \nfor policy makers as well as \nother stakeholders in the country including candidates, training providers, employers \netc..\n \nFurther, National Skill Development Mission (NSDM) has been launched to \nconverge and coordinate all efforts for Skill Development acro\nss the country.\n \n \n*****\n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|12|UNSTARRED |637", "t": "BSNL Satellite Phone Services", "head": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS  \nDEPARTMENT OF TELECOMMUNICATIONS  \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.637 \n TO BE ANSWERED ON 19th JULY, 2017 \n \nBSNL SATELLITE PHONE SERVICES \n \n†637.  SHRI SHER SINGH GHUBAYA:  \nDR. RAVINDRA KUMAR RAY: \n \nWill the Minister of COMMUNICATIONS be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether the Government has launched the BSNL satellite phone service;  \n \n(b) if so, the features of satellite phone and the departments/individuals likely to get \nthis facility in the first phase; and \n \n(c)  the time by which this service is likely to be launched in Punjab and Jharkhand \nalong with the details thereof ? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (IC) OF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS & \n MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n \n \n \n(a)  Bharat Sanchar Nigam Limited (BSNL) has launched Satellite Phone Services \nwith effect from 24.05.2017. \n(b) The satellite phone is equipped to provide voice and SMS services . The services \nwill be provided to Government users like Air Force, Army, State Police Departments, \nONGC, NTPC, Railway etc. Besides this, all existing satellite phone subscribers having \nvalid wireless operating license / No Objection Certificate (NOC) are  to be migrated to \nBSNL satellite phone service.  \n(c) Satellite Phone Service has been launched on PAN India basis. \n \n \n*************** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|12|UNSTARRED |638", "t": "DD and Radio Centres", "head": "        GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \n  MINISTRY OF INFORMATION & BROADCASTING \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION No. 638 \n(TO BE ANSWERED ON 19.07.2017) \n \nDD AND RADIO CENTRES  \n \n638. SHRI RAOSAHEB DANVE PATIL: \n \nWill the MINISTER OF INFORMATION AND BROADCASTING be pleased to \nstate: \n \n(a) the location and centre -wise total number of Doordarshan and Radio Centres \nfunctioning in the country;  \n(b) the location -wise, DD -wise and Radio Centre -wise details of upgradation  and \nmodernisation works undertaken in various Doordarshan and Radio Centres during \nthe last three years and the current year;  \n(c) the location -wise, Doordarshan and Radio Centre -wise details of the places not \nyet covered under the services of Doordarshan  and Radio Centres in the country \nand the reasons therefor; and  \n(d) the effective steps proposed to be taken by the Government in this regard?  \n                                                     ANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF INFORMATION AND \nBROADCASTING  \n{COL RAJYAVARDHAN RATHORE(Retd.)} \n \n(a) & (b)    Prasar Bharati has informed that as far as All India Radio(AIR) is \nconcerned, a s on date 421 Radio Broadcasting Centres are functioning in  the \ncountry.  Location and centre -wise details including up -gradation and modernization \nworks undertaken at  various Radio Centres during the last three yea rs and current \nyear are given at Annexure-I.  \n \nAs regards Doordarshan, at present  there are 67 Doordarshan Kendras (Studio \ncentres) and 1411 TV transmitters in Doordarshan network located in various parts \nof the country.  State/UT-wise and location -wise list of these centres is given at \nAnnexure-II.   Details of upgradation and modernization works undertaken in various \nDoordarshan centres during the last three years are given at Annexure-III.  \nLocation-wise details of major upgradation & modernization projects of Doordarshan \nwhich are currently at various stages of implementation are given at Annexure-IV. \n\n(c) & (d)  The present installed coverage capacity of AIR is about 92 % of the area \nand about 99 % of the total population of the country.  The present installed \ncoverage capacity of AIR FM is about 38 % by area and about 51 % by population of \nthe country. Some of the areas including hilly areas of Utt arakhand, Himachal \nPradesh & NE Regions are still uncovered by terrestrial AIR services. State -wise \ndetails of such uncovered areas by AIR service are given at Annexure-V. \n \n         It is pertinent to mention that 32  channels of All India Radio are available on \nDoordarshan’s DTH platform (DD Free Dish), which can be received by using DD \nfreedish set top Box throughout the country including uncovered areas. In  addition to \nthis, 13 popular channels of All India Radio can also be received through internet by \nbrowsing AIR’s website <allindiaradio.gov.in> and by downloading suitable apps on \niOS/ Android/ Windows based mobile phones. \n \nFollowing steps are proposed by AIR for strengthening & restoring AIR coverage in \nthe country: \n \n1.  Replacement of 6 nos. of old High Power MW transmitters by new state of art \ntechnology MW transmitter providing coverage in LWE affected areas. \n \n2.  Setting up of FM transmitters at 213 n ew locations across the country including \n100 W FM Relay transmitters (152 nos.) for localized coverage. \n \n3. Replacement/ up gradation of 77 nos. of old FM transmitters by new FM \ntransmitters. \n \n4. Provision f or providing 8 more channel on Doordarshan’s DTH platform (DD Free \nDish). \n \n5.  Provision of Live streaming of 7 additional AIR channels on Internet Platform. \n \n          AIR is in the process of expanding up 100 % FM coverage across the country \nfor which large amount of funds, other resources and skilled manpower would be \nrequired. Therefore, AIR is planning to set up  FM transmitter at new locations in \nphased manner under forthcoming schemes depending on availability of resources \nlike fund, manpower, land etc. \n \nAs regards Doordarshan, m ulti channel TV coverage of Doordarshan reaches all the \nareas of the country through Doordarshan’s free -to-air DTH service. It is possible to \nreceive DTH signals anywhere in the country with the help of a small sized dish \nreceive unit.   \n \nIn terrestrial mo de, TV coverage is estimated to be available to about 92% of \npopulation spread over 81% area of the country. In view of multi channel coverage \nhaving been provided to all the areas uncovered by terrestrial transmission along \nwith rest of the country, throu gh Doordarshan’s free -to-air DTH service, new \ntransmitters for expansion of terrestrial coverage are now not envisaged except a \nfew in border areas. \n***** \n\n \nANNEXURE AS REF ERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) &  (b) OF LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 638 FOR ANSWER ON 19.07.2017 \nANNEXURE -I \n \nList of Existing A.I.R. Stations along with modernization/ upgradation works \ncarried out /  undertaken during last three year & Current year \n \nS. \nNo. \n \nStatio"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|12|UNSTARRED |639", "t": "New Lines/Gauge Conversion/ Electrification", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 639 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 19.07.2017 \n \nNEW LINES/GAUGE CONVERSION/ELECTRIFICATION \n \n \n†639.  SHRI ARVIND SAWANT: \n \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n \n(a)  whether the Railways has conducted any survey for laying of \nnew rail lines, gauge conversion of old lines and \nelectrification in various States including Uttar Pradesh; \n \n(b)  if so, the details of the new rail lines to be laid, gauge \nconversion and the length of rail lines to be electrified in \nvarious States including Maharashtra, location-wise; \n \n(c)  the plan of the Government for laying of new rail lines, gauge \nconversion and electrification in the current financial year; \nand \n \n(d)  whether the Government proposes to construct a dedicated \ngoods corridor and if so, the details thereof ? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI RAJEN GOHAIN) \n \n \n(a) to (d):   A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n****** \n  \n\n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO ( d) OF UNSTARRED \nQUESTION NO. 639 BY SHRI ARVIND SAWANT TO BE ANSWERED IN LOK \nSABHA ON 19.07.2017 REGARDING NEW LINES/GAUGE CONVERSION/ \nELECTRIFICATION \n \n(a) & (b) : During the last three years and current year, Railways  have \nconducted 165 nos. for a total length of 19195 km of surveys for new lines, 9 \nnos. for gauge conversion for a total length of 541 km that includes State of \nUttar Pradesh. Details are as under:  \nS.No. Railway Zone No. of surveys conducted \nNew Line Gauge Conversion \n1 Central 9 0 \n2 East Coast 12 0 \n3 East Central 4 0 \n4 Eastern 0 0 \n5 North Central 11 0 \n6 North Eastern 4 1 \n7 Northeast Frontier 7 0 \n8 Northern 29 0 \n9 North Western 16 0 \n10 South Central 10 0 \n11 South East Central 25 0 \n12 South Eastern 2 0 \n13 Southern 16 0 \n14 South Western 8 0 \n15 West Central 2 0 \n16 Western  10 8 \n   165 9 \n  \nA total of 139 ongoing Railway Electrification projects totaling 28,431 \nRoute Km spread across the country in various States have been taken up  \nthat includes State of Maharashtra.  A total of 179 ongoing new line projects \ntotaling 20268 Km and 58 ongoing gauge conversion projects totaling 8152 \nKm have been taken up that includes the State of Maharashtra. Details of \nthese projects are available in  Pink Book laid on the Table of the House \nalongwith Budget Papers. \n \n\n \n(c):  In the current financial year 2017 -18, a total of 3500 Km of New Lines \nincluding DFC lines, Gauge Conversion, Doubling and 4000 Route Km of \nRailway Electrification have been planned/targeted.   \n \n(d):    Ministry of Railways have sanctioned implementation of Dedicated \nFreight Corridors (DFCs), namely, Western DFC (1504 Km) and Eastern DFC \n(1856 Km).   Western DFC starts from Jawaharlal Nehru Port Trust (JNPT), \nMumbai and passes through the States of Maharashtra, Gujarat, Rajasthan, \nHaryana and terminate at Dadri in Uttar Pradesh.  Eastern DFC starts from \nSahnewal near Ludhiana in Punjab and passes through the States of Haryana, \nUttar Pradesh, Bihar, Jharkhand and terminate at Dankuni in West Bengal.  \n \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|12|UNSTARRED |64", "t": "Export of Onions", "head": " \n \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF NEW AND RENEWABLE ENERGY \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 64 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2017 \n \nINSTALLATION OF SOLAR ROOFTOP SYSTEM \n \n*64. SHRI P.K.BIJU:   \n        SHRI KANWAR SINGH TANWAR:     \n                                                       \n Will the Minister of NEW AND RENEWABLE ENERGY be pleased to state: \n(a) the progress made in installati on of 4,200 MW solar rooftop system under the National \nSolar Mission with the budget of Rs.5000 crore allocated for the purpose in 2015;   \n     \n(b) whether the Government has kept any record of the numbers of houses in urban and rural \nareas which have rooftop solar panels supplying electricity and if so, the details thereof; and \n \n(c) the measures taken by the Government to  increase the number of solar rooftop project s \nin residential areas of the country? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR POWER, COAL, NEW & RENEWABLE ENERGY AND \nMINES (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) (SHRI PIYUSH GOYAL) \n(a) to (c ): A statement is laid on the table of the House  \n******* \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \nStatement \nStatement referred to reply to Part (a) to (c) of Lok Sabha \nStared Question No.64 to be answered on 20.07.2017 \nPart (a): An aggregate capacity of 671 MWp grid connected rooftop solar \nsystems have been installed in the country so far. Out of this 283MWp is in \nindustrial segment, 175MWp  in commercial segment, 79MWp in institutional \nsegment, 29 MWp in domestic household segment, 101MWp in Government \nsegment and 4MWp in social sector segment   \nPart (b): 3727 houses have installed rooftop solar systems under the scheme \nPart (C): To increase number of solar roof top projects in residential sector, \nthe Government inter alia has taken following measures: \n Central Financial Assistance  on bench mark cost is offered  for individual \nhouse holds to the tune of 30% in G eneral Category States and to the tune of \n70 % in Special Category States(North East States, Himachal Pradesh, \nJammu and Kashmir, Uttarkhand, Andaman and Nicobar islands and \nLakshadweep islands)  \n  States have been motivated to bring out net -metering regulations for grid \nconnected rooftop solar power plants  and as on today  all 3 6 States/UTs \nStates/ UTs have notified such regulations and/or tariff orders. \n 1933 firms have been empaneled as Channel Partners for easy reference by \nthe households for execution of grid connected rooftop solar projects. \n   In addition to State Nodal Agencies, Solar Energy Corporation of India \n(SECI)    has  been executing   roof top solar projects in residential / social / \ninstitutional  sectors. \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|12|UNSTARRED |640", "t": "Advocates (Amendment) Bill, 2017", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF LAW & JUSTICE\nDEPARTMENT OF LEGAL AFFAIRS\n*****\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 640\nTO BE ANSWERED ON 19.07.2017\nAdvocates (Amendment) Bill, 2017\n640. SHRI HUKUM SINGH:\nWill the Minister of LAW AND JUSTICE be pleased to state:\n(a) whether lawyers are against the recommendations of the Advocates (Amendment) \nBill, 2017 and if so, the details thereof and the reasons therefor; \n(b) whether the said Bill is likely to take away the autonomy of all the bar councils \nand associations; and\n(c) if so, the details thereof and the reasons therefor?\nANSWER\nMINISTER OF STATE FOR LAW AND JUSTICE AND ELECTRONICS AND \nINFORMATION TECHNOLOGY\n(SHRI P.P. CHAUDHARY)\n(a) to (c) : The Law Commission of India submitted its Report No. 266 titled “The \nAdvocates Act, 1961 (Regulation of Legal Profession)” for consideration by the \nGovernment” on 23.03.2017 with reference to direction of Hon’ble Supreme \nCourt in “Mahipal Singh Rana Vs State of U.P. (AIR 2016 SC 3302). The Law \nCommission has also prepared a Bill namely “the Advocates (Amendment) Bill, \n2017” as Annexure-III of the report.\nThe Department of Legal Affairs sought views/comments of the Bar Council of \nIndia and all the State Bar Councils, Bar Associations of all the High Courts \nincluding Supreme Court of India. In this regard response from the Bar Council of \nIndia, various State Bar Councils and various Bar Associations of the High Courts \nhave been received. Apart from this, the Department of Legal Affairs has received \nrepresentations from various District Bar Associations, Advocate’s Associations, \nIndividuals from all over country.\nAll the responses/representations which have been received in this Department \ninter-alia reflect that they are opposing the Report No. 266 th of the Law \nCommission of India on the grounds that the proposed Bill recommends for \nintroducing non-legal persons entering into the Statutory Body in the name of \neminent persons and they will be empowered to deal with the disciplinary \nproceedings against the Advocates.\n**********"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|12|UNSTARRED |641", "t": "Data of Officers", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.641 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 19.07.2017 \n \nDATA OF OFFICERS \n641.    SHRI VINOD LAKHAMASHI CHAVDA : \n    \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state : \n(a) whether the Government has any data of officers working \nat the same position in western division; and \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof, division-wise including \nAhmedabad division? \n  \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI RAJEN GOHAIN) \n \n(a) & (b) : Officers working on sensitive posts for longer than 3  to \n4 years are transferred as per the prescribed transfer/rotation \npolicy.      \n****** \n             \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|12|UNSTARRED |642", "t": "Socio-Economic Development of NER", "head": "Government of India \nMinistry of Development of North Eastern Region  \n \nLOK SABHA \nUnstarred Question No. 642 \n \nTo be answered on \nWednesday, July 19, 2017/Ashadha 28, 1939 (Saka) \n \nQuestion \nSocio-Economic Development of NER  \n642.   SHRI RABINDRA KUMAR JENA : \n  Will the Minister of DEVELOPMENT OF NORTH EASTERN  REGION be \npleased to state: \n(a)  whether the Government has taken any major pol icy decisions for socio-\neconomic development of the North Eastern Region (N ER) and if so, the details \nthereof; \n(b)  the details of projects financed by the North Eastern Development Finance \nCorporation Limited (NEDFCL) and the funds allocate d/utilised during each of the \nlast three years and the current year, project-wise; \n(c)  whether the NEDFCL has scaled down disbursemen t target from the financial \nyear 2013-14 and if so, the details thereof and the reasons therefor; and \n(d)  the other steps being taken by the Government for economic development of \nNorth Eastern Region? \n \nANSWER \nThe Minister of State (Independent Charge) of the Ministry of Development \nof \nNorth Eastern Region \n        [Dr. Jitendra Singh] \n \n \n(a)    The Government had enhanced the earmarked ou tlay from Rs.29124.79 crore \nat BE stage in 2016-17 to Rs.32180.08 crore at the RE stage to be spent by Fifty Six \n(56) line Ministries in the North Eastern Region. T his has been further increased by \n34.38% to Rs.43244.64 crore in 2017-18 \n. \n \n \n \n \n\n(b)      The details of projects financed by the North Easte rn Development Finance \nCorporation Limited (NEDFi) and the funds allocated / utilised during each of the last \nthree years and the current year, project-wise are as follows: \n \nFunds allocated/ utilized during last three years and current year  \n(Amount in Rs. crore ) \nYear \nFund \nreceived \nfrom GoI \nUtilization of \nfund received \nfrom GoI \nNorth Eastern \nDevelopment \nFinance Corporation \nLimited (NEDFi's ) \nOwn Fund/Market \nBorrowings  \nTotal \nDisbursement \n2014 -15  60.00 60.00 327.20 387.20 \n2015 -16  30.00 30.00 272.99 302.99 \n2016 -17  30.00 30.00 319.09 349.09 \n2017 -18  - - 31.08 31.08 \n \nList of projects funded during the above period is annexed.  \n  \n \n(c)      No, Madam.  \n(d) As stated in part (a) above. \n \n***** \n  \n\nAnnexure \nAnnexure refer to in reply to part (b) of Lok Sabha Unstarred Question No. 642 for answer on 19.07.2017. \n \nNorth Eastern Development Finance Corporation Ltd. \nUtilisation of Ministry of Development of North Eastern Region fund in MSME in FY 2014-15 \n \nARUNACHAL PRADESH:                            \n(Rs. in lakh)  \nS. No.  Unit  District  Scheme  Disbursement  Project  \n1 Pine Ridge Yath  Lower Subansiri  RTL  10.00  Tourist Resort  \n2 Lathao Bricks  Lohit  NOSSE  6.00  Bricks  \n3 NIBA Hospital  Papumpare  NOSSE  95.00  Hospital  \n4 OG Enterprise Papumpare WEDS 2.00 Readymade Garment \nShowroom  \n5 Rinjin Cloth Shop  Papumpare  WEDS  2.00  Readymade Garments  \n6 PS Collection  Papumpare  WEDS  1.00  Readymade Garments  \n7 Abotani bell metal_2nd Papumpare WEDS 2.00 Expansion Of Existing Bell \nMetal Industry  \n8 The Chop Shop Papumpare NEEDS 1.01 Tender Meat Processing \nShop  \n9 Golden Crown Restaurant (II)  Papumpare  NEEDS  5.00  Restaurant  \n10  10 Tenz Restaurant  Papumpare  WEDS  5.00  Restaurant  \n11  Sargam Academy (II)  Papumpare  WEDS  5.00  Dance Institute  \n12  Kids Zone  Papumpare  WEDS  5.00  Kids Wear  \n13  Dalha Shop  Papumpare  WEDS  5.00  Readymade Garments  \n14  Itafort Cloth Store  Papumpare  WEDS  5.00  Readymade Garments  \n15  Lekhi Public School  Papumpare  NOSSE  100.00  School  \n16 DD Readymade Garments \n(II)  Papumpare WEDS 5.00 Readymade Garments \n17  Anju Cloth Store  Papumpare  WEDS  5.00  Readymade Garments  \n18  Sun View Restaurant  Papumpare  WEDS  5.00  Restaurant  \n19  New Fashion (II)  Papumpare  WEDS  5.00  Readymade Garments  \n20  Langle Enterprise  Papumpare  WEDS  1.50  Grocery  \n21  3R & Anjoli Grocery  Papumpare  WEDS  3.50  Grocery  \n22  Seven Star (ii)  Papumpare  WEDS  5.00  Readymade Garments  \n23  Singyong Rhee Shop (ii)  Papumpare  WEDS  5.00  Readymade Garments  \n24  MK Enterprises  Papumpare  WEDS  5.00  Readymade Garments  \n25  Butterflies  Papumpare  NEEDS  4.00  Preschool  \n26  R D Chukla Enterprise  Papumpare  WEDS  5.00  Readymade Garments  \n27  Rashmi Cloth House -3rd  Papumpare  WEDS  5.00  Readymade Garments  \n28  Waistline  Papumpare  WEDS  5.00  Readymade Garments  \n29  Kal's Collection -2nd  Papumpare  WEDS  5.00  Garments Shop  \n30  T T Traders  Papumpare  WEDS  5.00  Men's Clothing Shop  \n31  MY Shop - 2nd  Papumpare  WEDS  5.00  Readymade Garments Shop  \n32 Yamang Rina Cane Bamboo \n& Wooden Industries  Passighat SNEHH 5.00 Cane And Bamboo Wooden \nFurniture  \n33  Fast Food Corner  Papumpare  WEDS  5.00  Fast Food Centre  \n34  Glamour fashions  Papumpare  WEDS  5.00  Readymade Garment Shop  \n35  Modern Fashion corner  Papumpare  WEDS  5.00  Readymade Garment Shop  \n36  Pacific Beauty Salon  Papumpre  WEDS  4.00  Beauty Salon  \n37  Next World "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|12|UNSTARRED |643", "t": "Decrease in Tatkal Quota Seats", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.643 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 19.07.2017 \n \nDECREASE IN TATKAL QUOTA SEATS \n \n†643.  SHRI SUKHBIR SINGH JAUNAPURIA:  \n       \n           Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government is considering to increase or decrease \nthe number of seats in all the trains under the Tatkal Scheme; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n \n(c) whether the Government is formulating any such  scheme to \nenable the passenger  to travel even on unconfirmed ticket booked \nagainst tatkal quota so that passenger can do his important work on \ntime or reach home on time; and \n \n(d) if so, the details thereof?   \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI RAJEN GOHAIN) \n \n(a) & (b): Instructions have been issued to Zonal Railways to earmark \nup to 30% of the accommodation as Tatkal.  However, the actual \nextent of accommodation to be earmarked under Tatkal scheme is \ndecided by Zonal Railways on  the basis of demand pattern and \navailability of accommodation. Tatkal quota so earmarked is \nreviewed on periodical basis and adjustments made, wherever \nrequired based on utilization subject to maximum limit mentioned \nabove. This is a continuous process. \n \n(c) : No, Madam. \n \n(d) : Does not arise. \n****** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|12|UNSTARRED |644", "t": "Frequency of Train", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 644 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 19.07.2017 \n \nFREQUENCY OF TRAIN \n \n644.  PROF. K.V.THOMAS: \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether there is a train running between Ernakulam and \nRameshwaram daily;  \n \n(b) if so, whether there is any proposal to discontinue this train; and \n \n(c) if so, the reasons therefor? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI RAJEN GOHAIN) \n \n \n(a): No, Madam.  There is no train running between Ernakulam and \nRameshwaram daily.  \n \n(b) & (c): Do not arise. \n \n \n***** \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|12|UNSTARRED |645", "t": "Accidents due to Railway Tracks", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.645 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 19.07.2017 \n \nACCIDENTS DUE TO RAILWAY TRACKS \n \n†645.   SHRIMATI VEENA DEVI: \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether a large number of train accidents have occurred due to \nshort-comings of railway tracks during the years 2014 -15, 2015-16 \nand 2016-17; \n \n(b) if so, the number of such train accidents during the above period; \n \n(c) whether it has become necessary for t he Railways to replace the \ntracks; \n \n(d) if so, the length of railway tracks in terms of kilometres that has \nbeen considered necessary to be replaced; and \n \n(e) the length of railway tracks in terms of kilometres  that has been \nreplaced during each of the above years?  \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n(SHRI RAJEN GOHAIN) \n \n \n(a) to (e):  A Statement is laid on the Table of  the House. \n \n***** \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (e) OF \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 645 BY SHRIMATI VEENA DEVI TO BE \nANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 19.07.2017 REGARDING ACCIDENTS \nDUE TO RAILWAY TRACKS \n \n(a) & (b): Consequential train accidents have occurred due to various \nfactors, one of them is shortcomings of Railway track. Consequential \ntrain accidents occurred  on account of track shortcomings during the \nyears 2014-15, 2015-16 and 2016-17  are as under : \nYear 2014-15 2015-16 2016-17 \nNumber of accidents occurred \ndue to shortcomings of \nRailway track \n \n21 \n \n24 \n \n35 \n \n(c) to (e): Track renewal is a continuous activity, which is undertaken \nas and when a stretch become s due for renewal as per criteria laid \ndown in para  302 of Indian Railway Permanent Way Manual (IRPWM) \nwhich, inter-alia, takes into account the traffic carried over the track, \nincidence of rail fractures/failures, wear, age, etc.  The details of track \nrenewal targeted and carried out in the last three years are as under : \nYear Target (in KM) Track Renewed (in KM) \n2014-15 2200 2424 \n2015-16 2500 2794 \n2016-17 2668 2487 \n \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|12|UNSTARRED |646", "t": "Monitoring of Projects in Chhattisgarh", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF STATISTICS AND PROGRAMME IMPLEMENTATION \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.646 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON WEDNESDAY, THE 19th JULY, 2017 \n \nMONITORING OF PROJECTS IN CHHATTISGARH \n \n646. SHRILAKHAN LAL SAHU: \n \nWill the Minister of STATISTICS AND PROGRAMME \nIMPLEMENTATION be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government is keeping vigil over the various \nrunning central projects in Chhattisgarh; \n(b) the time by which the aforementioned projectsare likely to be \ncompleted; \n(c) the details of new projects proposed to be started in \nChhattisgarh during the last three years; and \n(d) the amount proposed to be allocated to each such project? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATISTICS AND PROGRAMME IMPLEMENTATION [SHRI \nD.V. SADANANDA GOWDA] \n \n(a)& (b): Government through the Ministry of Statistics and Programme \nImplementation monitors on -going central sector infrastructure projects \ncosting Rs. 150 crore and above on time and cost overruns through its \nonline computeriz ed monitoring system (OCMS) on the basis \nofinformation provided by the project implementation agencies. As on \n01.04.2017, 42on-going central sectorprojects costing Rs. 150 crore and \nabovewere in the state of Ch hattisgarh. Details of p roject-\nwiseanticipated d ate of completion as provided by the respective \nproject implementing agencyis at Annexure-I. \n \n(c)& (d): Details of new central sector projects costing Rs 150 crore and \nabove which were approved during the last three years along with the \nanticipated cost as reported by the project implementing agencies  is at \nAnnexure–II. \n\n                                                                   Annexure- I \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) & (b) OF LOK SABHA  UNSTARRED QUESTION NO 646 DUE FOR \nANSWER ON  19.07.2017 \nDETAILS OF ONGOING CENTRAL SECTOR PROJECTS COSTING Rs. 150 CRORE AND ABOVE IN CHATTISGARH (as on \n01.04.2017) \nSr \nNo. PROJECT NAME \nDATE OF \nAPPROV\nAL \nORIGINAL \nDATE OF \nCOMMISSIONI\nNG \nANTICIPATED \nDATE OF \nCOMMISSIONI\nNG \nORIGIN\nAL \nCOST \n(Rs in \ncrore) \nANTICIPAT\nED COST \n(Rs in \ncrore) \nCOST \nOVERRU\nN (Rs in \ncrore) \nTIME \nOVERR\nUN (in \nmonths) \n1 \nJAGANNATHPOR \nOCP(3.00MTY)                                                                            09/2008 03/2015 03/2020 152 460 202 60 \n2 \nAMLAI OC \nEXPANSION SECTOR  \nB (1.50 MTY)                                                              11/2009 03/2016 03/2018 199 199 0 24 \n3 \nKARTALI (EAST) OCP \n(2.50 MTY)                                                                        07/2008 03/2014 03/2020 178 178 0 72 \n4 \nPELMA \nOCP(15.00MTY)                                                                                  11/2014 03/2023 03/2023 1,625 1,625 0 0 \n5 AMERA OC RCE                                                                           