\nWill the Minister of  DRINKING WATER AND SANITATION be pleased to state : \n(a) whether new toilets have been constructed in the rural areas under Swachh Bharat Mission \n(SBM) in the country during the last three years; \n(b) if so, the total number thereof; \n(c) whether due to the use of more additional toile ts, the problem of solid sewage and water \nhas become more complex in villages; \n(d) if so, the reaction of the Government thereto; and  \n(e) the number of villages where the system for the  disposal of polluted water and human \nexcreta has been installed during the last three years and the capacity of the said system? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR MINISTRY OF DRINKING WATER & SANITATION \n(SHRI RAMESH CHANDAPPA JIGAJINAGI) \n \n(a) Yes, Madam. \n \n(b) Number of Individual household latrines (IHHLs)  constructed under Swachh Bharat \nMission (Gramin) during last three years is as under :-  \n \nS.N. Year No. of IHHLs constructed \n1 2014-15 58,39,644  \n2 2015-16 1,26,92,253  \n3 2016-17 2,19,21,164  \n \n(c) to (d) \nUnder Swachh Bharat Mission (Gramin), measures are taken to prevent open \ndefecation and to provide safe disposal of human ex creta. This can be done through on-site \ntoilet technologies such as twin-leach pit that do not require underground sewerage system \nand are much cheaper and equally effective.  \n \n(e) Solid and Liquid Waste Management (SLWM) is one  of the integral components of \nSBM(G) and under Liquid Waste Management, activitie s like low cost drainage, soakage \nchannels/ pits, waste stabilization ponds system, r euse of waste water etc. can be taken up. \nDepending upon the amount of waste water generated,  the State can choose the type of liquid \nwaste management facility they wish to create. Fund s for Solid and Liquid Waste \nManagement activities with a cap of Rs. 7/12/15/20 lakh are available for Gram Panchayats \nhaving upto 150/300/500/ more than 500 households. \n \n \n\n \n \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|12|UNSTARRED |873", "t": "Highway Projects in Abroad", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.873 \nANSWERED ON 20th JULY, 2017 \n \nHIGHWAY PROJECTS IN ABROAD  \n873.  SHRI GEORGE BAKER:  \nPROF. RICHARD HAY:  \n \nWill the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS  be pleased to state: \nसड़क परिवहन औि िाजमार्ग मंत्री \n(a)  whether the Government is planning to launch a dedicated international subsidiary \nof the National Highways Authority of India to take up roads and highway projects \nabroad, particularly in South Asia;  \n(b)  if so, the details thereof, country-wise;  \n(c)  the details of the funds likely to be sanctioned for this along with the target set; and  \n(d)  the time by which is likely to be started?  \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \n(SHRI PON. RADHAKRISHNAN) \n \n \n(a) & (d) Government had set up a Committee to examine the concept of establishing \nan Indian Entity for taking up road and construction projects abroad.  The Committee has \nsubmitted its report.  The Report is under consideration. \n \n \n****** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|12|UNSTARRED |874", "t": "NH in Kerala", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 874 \nANSWERED ON 20TH JULY, 2017 \n \nNH IN KERALA \n \n874.  SHRI N.K. PREMACHANDRAN: \n SHRI P.K. BIJU: \n \nWill the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \nसड़क परिवहन औि िाजमार्ग मंत्री \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government proposes to give priority for development  of National Highways, if so, \nthe details thereof State-wise along with the number of NHs in Kerala; \n(b) the details of fund allocated for  development of National Highways during  the last three years, \nState-wise; \n(c) the details of funds utilization  report from the Central and State  Governments since 2015 \nregarding construction/maintenance of these NHs; \n(d) the details regarding the present status of Kollam Bye-pass in Kerala; and \n(e) the proposed date of completion of Kollam Bye-pass? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE  \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \n(SHRI PON. RADHAKRISHNAN) \n \n(a)  The development and maintenance of National Highways ( NHs) is a continuous process. \nThe works on NHs in the country, including those in the State of Kerala, are, accordingly, taken up \nfrom time to time as per inter-se priority, traffic density and availability of funds to keep the NHs in \ntraffic worthy conditions. \n \n The Ministry has taken up development of NHs under various phases of National Highways \nDevelopment Project (NHDP), Special Accelerated Road Development Programme for the North \nEast Region (SARDP-NE) including Arunachal Pradesh Package of Roads, Specia l Programme for \nDevelopment of Roads in the Left Wing Extremism (LWE) affected areas, National Highways \nInterconnectivity Improvement Project (NHIIP), etc. \n  \nState/ Union Territory (UT) –wise details of NHs are at Annexure-I. \n \n(b) and (c)   State/ UT –wise details of allocation and expenditure for development and \nMaintenance and R epair (M&R) of NHs during the last three years  and current year  are at \nAnnexure-II. The expenditure reported has been incurred for the purpose for which allocation s \nwere made. \n \n(d)  The physical progress of Kollam bypass  is about 61% till date. \n(e) The target date of completion of Kollam bypass is August, 2018.  \n \n\nANNEXURE-I \nANNEXURE REFERRED IN REPLY TO PART  (a) OF LOK SABHA UNSTARRED \nQUESTION NO. 874 ANSWERED ON 20.07.2017 ASKED BY SHRI N.K.  \nPREMACHANDRAN AND SHRI P.K. BIJU REGARDING NH IN KERALA  \nState/ UT –wise details of NHs \nSl. \nNo. \nName of \nState/ UT \nNational Highway No. Total Length \n(in km) \n1 Andhra \nPradesh  \n16 G.Q., 216, 216A, 716, 26, 326, 326A, 30, 40, 140, 42, 44 N.S., 65, 165, 365 BB, \n565, 67, 69, 71, 75, 340