27) (127) (200) (200) (192) (192) (192) (192) \n  Nagaland Nagaland PD (179) (179)"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|12|UNSTARRED |902", "t": "Fund Record of RGSA", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF PANCHAYATI RAJ \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 902 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2017 \n \nFUND RECORD OF RGSA \n \n902. SHRI ANTO ANTONY: \n  \n Will the Minister of PANCHAYATI RAJ be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government has any record regarding fund allocated for the capacity \nbuilding of the Panchayati Raj Institutions (PRIs) under the Rashtriya Gram Swaraj \nAbhiyan (RGSA) during the last two years; \n(b) if so, the details thereof, State-wise and year-wise; \n(c) whether it is a fact that the Government has received proposals from various State \nGovernments including Kerala regarding the enhancement of financial allocation under \nthe RGSA; and \n(d) if so, the details thereof and the response of the Government thereto? \n \n \nANSWER \n \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF PANCHAYATI RAJ \n(SHRI PARSHOTTAM RUPALA) \n \n \n(a) & (b):  Yes. The details of the fund allocated for capacity building of the Panchayati \nRaj Institutions (PRIs) under the RGSA during last two years are provided in Annexure.   \n \n(c) & (d):  Proposals for financial assistance under the scheme of RGSA have been \nreceived from 14 States including Kerala during the current financial year and considered and \napproved by Central Executive Committee of RGSA. Details of the fund sanctioned to States \nduring the year 2017-18 (till 17/07/2017) are given in Annexure and there is enhancement of \nthe sanctioned fund to many States including Kerala.   \n \n \n \n  \n\nAnnexure \n \nPosition regarding State-wise funds sanctioned and released under CB-PSA/RGSA \nduring 2015-16 to 2016-17 and 2017-18 (as on 17.07.2017) \n (Amount Rs. in Cr.) \nSL.\nNo. \nName of the \nState/ UTs \n2015-16 2016-17 2017-18 \nSancti\noned \nFunds \nReleas\ned \nSanctione\nd \nFunds \nReleased \nS