d period; \n(c) the details of the width and length  of each of those roads in respect of which  the construction \nwork had been completed; \n(d) the details of the names of those  States where the construction work for widening the National \nHighways is going on; and \n(e) the funds allocated to these during the last three years, State-wise? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE  \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \n(SHRI PON. RADHAKRISHNAN) \n \n(a) and (b) The total length of National Highways (NHs) in the country during the last two years \nand the current year along with the number of kilometres added are as follows:- \nDetails Year \n2015-16 2016-17 2017-18* \nLength of NHs added (km) 3,180 13,148 1,277 \nTotal Length of NHs (km) 1,01,010 1,14,158 1,15,435 \n*-Status as on 30.06.2017. \n \n(c) and (d) Development and maintenance of NHs is a continuous process. The works on NHs \nare, accordingly, carried out as per inter-se priority, traffic density and availability of funds. \n \nThe details of development of NHs in terms of widening to two lane/ four lane NH standards \nor more during the last two years and the current year are as follows:- \n \nLength in km \nLane 2015-16 2016-17 2017-18* \nWidening to Two Lane NH Standards 3,970 5,060 1,155 \nWidening to Four Lane NH Standards 1,010 1,655 466 \nWidening to more than Four Lane NH Standards 279 167 28 \n*-Status as on 30.06.2017. \n \n State/ Union Territory (UT) –wise details of NHs are at Annexure-I. Works for widening of \nNHs are going on in the States/ UTs mentioned at Annexure-I, except for the UTs of Daman & Diu, \nDadra & Nagar Haveli and Chandigarh. \n \n(e)  State/ UT–wise details of funds allocated for development of NHs during the last three years \nare at Annexure-II. \n\nANNEXURE-I \nANNEXURE REFERRED IN REPLY TO PARTS (c) AND  (d) OF LOK SABHA UNSTARRED \nQUESTION NO. 918 ANSWERED ON 20.07.2017 ASKED BY SHRI RAJU SHETTY  AND \nSHRI AJAY MISRA TENI REGARDING LENGTH OF NHS \n